From 06447ab9bf465d9b708eeb28e41677373888e7af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 09:18:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: every Reaper page now links to its section of the
 owner's guide

Twelve pages gained the "?" help link in their heading: QoS, QoS Diagnostics,
Traffic Analyzer, Devices, Connections, Wireless, WiFi Professional,
Diagnostics, Firmware, Analytics, Policy Routing and AI Advisor. Firewall,
Gatekeeper, Warden, Storage and USB already had one; About and First Boot link
to the guide root, which is right for those two; BackupCard is an injected card
with no heading of its own.

This reuses the established pagehead pattern exactly - an inline-styled anchor
inside the h1, target=_blank with rel=noopener noreferrer, title and aria from
the existing shared RABT_43 key. Consequences worth noting:

- ZERO new i18n keys. RABT_43 ("Owner's Guide") is already present in all 25
  packs, so the dict lockstep is untouched at 6745 lines and no translation
  pass is owed for this change.
- Rule 29 checked: RABT_43 lands in a double-quoted title attribute, and no
  pack's translation of it contains a double quote (0/25). It carries an
  apostrophe, which is safe in a dq attribute and is how the five existing
  pages already use it.
- No new CSS. The pagehead pattern is self-styled inline; the .helpdot /
  .tabintro CSS stays confined to the two pages that use per-tab buttons.

Three pages (QoS Diagnostics, Connections, WiFi Professional) put their heading
in .stickytop > .appbar rather than .pagehead, so the insertion matches either
container and anchors on the first </h1> after it.

All 15 distinct anchors now referenced by the firmware were verified to exist
as headings in docs/REAPER-GUIDE.md, against origin/main - the guide was pushed
first precisely so these resolve on the first boot that carries them, rather
than 404-ing until a later push.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
